-- Demonology (Diabolist), transcribed from the simc `diabolist` list.
--
-- The on-disk twin of the `demonology-diabolist` profile the addon ships. Each glow is one
-- APL line with the terms the addon cannot read dropped, so a lit icon means "this line's
-- readable conditions hold" and never "cast this now": priority ORDER is not expressible.
--
-- Check it, or turn it into a share string:
--     uv run python -m wowkb.smartglo check  projects/smart-glo/rules/demonology-diabolist.sg
--     uv run python -m wowkb.smartglo encode projects/smart-glo/rules/demonology-diabolist.sg

spec demonology

-- ⚠ Every shard threshold below reads `.after_cast`, which is the count as it will stand once
-- the cast in flight lands. Shards are debited at COMPLETION, so mid-cast the bar still shows
-- the pre-cast number and a plain threshold answers about a state that is already gone: at 5
-- shards casting Hand of Gul'dan it keeps saying "capped" for the whole cast, and stops
-- saying it exactly when the answer becomes useful. The projection subtracts the cost and
-- adds the gain at the same moment, because both land at the same moment.
--
-- Demonology is the spec this works for. `soul_shards` is the only resource the addon lets a
-- rule project past a cast, because it is the only one whose per-cast amounts are whole and
-- invariant -- Holy Power and Combo Point gains move with talents and procs, and the Tier-1
-- energize rows say so (knowledge/classes/_abilities/power-gain.tsv).
--
-- Nothing casting is a projection of ZERO, not an unknown, so these read exactly like plain
-- thresholds while you stand still.

-- ⚠ An APL line is only reachable when its spell is castable, so simc never writes that
-- condition down. A GLOW has no such implicit: `Attach.Evaluate` lights a mark on the rule's
-- own terms and nothing else, and the only other suppressor is whether the row is visible --
-- which a cooldown row is, all the way through its sweep. So every rung on a spell with a
-- cooldown carries `ready()` here, and the ones that do not are the spells that have none.

-- `summon_demonic_tyrant,if=soul_shard=5`. The APL also wants the Grimoires and Dreadstalkers
-- already spent, but it says so by ORDER -- they sit above this line -- and order is the one
-- thing a rule surface cannot say. `not ready(...)` on the two summons whose demons Tyrant
-- actually counts is the readable form of the same thought, and it is the stricter half:
-- it holds Tyrant rather than leaking it.
--
-- Not urgent. Tyrant at cap is a rhythm, not a proc window closing.
glow "Tyrant at five shards"
  on     summon_demonic_tyrant
  when   ready(summon_demonic_tyrant) and not ready(call_dreadstalkers) and not ready(grimoire_imp_lord) and soul_shards.after_cast == 5

-- `hand_of_guldan,if=...|soul_shard=5` -- the unconditional half. At cap the shard is lost
-- otherwise, so nothing outranks the dump.
glow "Hand of Gul'dan capped"
  on     hand_of_guldan
  when   soul_shards.after_cast == 5
  urgent

-- `hand_of_guldan,if=soul_shard>=3&cooldown.summon_demonic_tyrant.remains>5`. The two halves
-- travel together: THREE is only safe because of the Tyrant guard, which is what stops the
-- spend band from eating the shards Tyrant wants. An earlier pass kept neither and used Icy
-- Veins' looser "4-5 Soul Shards" instead, which spends into the window this holds for.
--
-- `>` is false at zero remaining, so a ready Tyrant silences this rung on its own -- no
-- `not ready()` guard needed, and none of the true-at-zero trouble the `<` forms carry.
glow "Hand of Gul'dan outside the Tyrant hold"
  on     hand_of_guldan
  when   soul_shards.after_cast >= 3
  bind   summon_demonic_tyrant.cooldown > 5s

-- Dominion of Argus's window IS the Tyrant window, so this aura is the only way the addon
-- has to ask "is Tyrant out". The id is the tracked Cooldown Manager row, not the talent
-- 1276163: the talent id names no row, so a latch on it would read UNKNOWN forever.
glow "Hand of Gul'dan inside the Argus window"
  on     hand_of_guldan
  when   aura(dominion_of_argus)

-- `demonbolt,if=soul_shard<4&buff.demonic_core.react` -- any Core, below the shard ceiling.
glow "Demonbolt on a Core below four shards"
  on     demonbolt
  when   soul_shards.after_cast < 4 and aura(demonic_core)

-- Not an APL rung: the APL never counts Cores, it only asks whether one is up. This is the
-- OVERCAP rung. Demonic Core caps at 4 and the guide's own warning is that pooling past 2
-- risks losing stacks, so 4 is the point where the next proc is already gone. Urgent because
-- unlike the rung above, waiting here costs something outright.
glow "Demonbolt at Core cap"
  on     demonbolt
  bind   demonic_core.stacks >= 4
  urgent

-- Infernal Bolt is a Mother of Chaos PROC, so its row exists only inside the proc window --
-- which is why this glow carries no gate of its own beyond the shard count.
glow "Infernal Bolt below three shards"
  on     infernal_bolt
  when   soul_shards.after_cast < 3

-- `shadow_bolt` -- the filler, and the rung the whole list falls through to. The readable
-- form of "you need shards and Demonbolt is not available" is the shard count plus the
-- absence of a Core; a refused or untracked Core latch reads UNKNOWN and this fails dark,
-- which is the right way round for a filler.
--
-- ⚠ Shadow Bolt and Infernal Bolt SHARE a row: the proc swaps the spell and keeps the
-- cooldownID (Attach.lua:456), which is why Infernal Bolt has a row to appear on at all.
-- So this glow and the rung above paint the same icon, and they overlap below 3 shards with
-- no Core. Whether `on shadow_bolt` still binds while the row is showing Infernal Bolt is an
-- in-game question -- see the test list at the foot of this file.
glow "Shadow Bolt with no Core"
  on     shadow_bolt
  when   soul_shards.after_cast < 5 and not aura(demonic_core)

-- `implosion,if=buff.wild_imps.stack>=6&(active_enemies>2|talent.to_hell_and_back.enabled)`.
-- Enemy count is not readable, but the talent is -- and it is the half that matters here,
-- because without To Hell and Back the guide is flat that Implosion is never worth casting
-- single target. Dropping BOTH halves, as an earlier pass did, lit this on six imps against
-- one target, which is the spec's classic damage loss.
glow "Implosion at six imps"
  on     implosion
  when   ready(implosion) and talent(to_hell_and_back)
  bind   wild_imp.stacks >= 6
  urgent

glow "Ruination"
  on     ruination
  when   ready(ruination)

glow "Grimoire: Imp Lord"
  on     grimoire_imp_lord
  when   ready(grimoire_imp_lord)

glow "Grimoire: Fel Ravager"
  on     grimoire_fel_ravager
  when   ready(grimoire_fel_ravager)

glow "Summon Doomguard"
  on     summon_doomguard
  when   ready(summon_doomguard)

-- ------------------------------------------------------- Call Dreadstalkers, all four rungs

-- The APL has two Dreadstalkers lines and the talent picks which one is live:
--
--   call_dreadstalkers,if=talent.reign_of_tyranny&(cooldown.summon_demonic_tyrant.remains>=20+gcd.max
--                                                 |cooldown.summon_demonic_tyrant.remains<=12-gcd.max)
--   call_dreadstalkers,if=!talent.reign_of_tyranny
--
-- Reign of Tyranny banks imps for the Tyrant, so with it taken the dogs are held through the
-- 12..20s band and sent at either end. Without it there is no window at all.

glow "Call Dreadstalkers without Reign of Tyranny"
  on     call_dreadstalkers
  when   not talent(reign_of_tyranny) and ready(call_dreadstalkers)

-- The far end, `remains>=20+gcd.max`. Urgent: this is the send that has to happen before the
-- band closes, and missing it costs the dogs their place in the next Tyrant.
glow "Dreadstalkers with Tyrant far off"
  on     call_dreadstalkers
  when   talent(reign_of_tyranny) and ready(call_dreadstalkers)
  bind   summon_demonic_tyrant.cooldown > 20s
  urgent

-- The near end, `remains<=12-gcd.max`, split in TWO -- and the split is what makes it
-- expressible rather than a workaround.
--
-- `<` on a cooldown is also true at zero remaining, so `Rules.lua:192` refuses it without a
-- `not ready()` guard. Here that refusal points at something real: the APL's `<=12` is
-- deliberately true when Tyrant is UP, and a rule that bolted on the guard to satisfy the
-- checker would go dark exactly when the dogs matter most. So the zero case gets its own
-- glow, which needs no sealed leaf at all, and the running case gets the bind with an honest
-- guard -- it only ever speaks while a cooldown is actually running.
--
-- Together they cover `remains <= 12` with no gap and no dishonest term, and the 12..20s
-- band stays dark on all four rungs, which IS the hold.
glow "Dreadstalkers into the Tyrant window"
  on     call_dreadstalkers
  when   talent(reign_of_tyranny) and ready(call_dreadstalkers) and not ready(summon_demonic_tyrant)
  bind   summon_demonic_tyrant.cooldown < 12s

glow "Dreadstalkers with Tyrant ready"
  on     call_dreadstalkers
  when   talent(reign_of_tyranny) and ready(call_dreadstalkers) and ready(summon_demonic_tyrant)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- Power Siphon

-- `power_siphon,if=buff.demonic_core.stack<=1`. ⚠ That gate is NOT expressible: a count bind
-- reads `>= n` only (Parse.lua:232), because the client paints it by taking an occluder away
-- at the threshold, and there is no inverse. An at-most count has no form here.
--
-- So the shipped gate is the imp count -- the other half of the same decision, from the Icy
-- Veins rung ("2 or less Demonic Core and at least 2 Wild Imps out"): Power Siphon converts
-- imps into Cores, so imps out is its precondition either way. The Core ceiling is DROPPED
-- rather than approximated, which means this can light while you are already Core-rich.
glow "Power Siphon with imps out"
  on     power_siphon
  when   ready(power_siphon)
  bind   wild_imp.stacks >= 2

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------ confirm while logged in
--
--   * Ruination reportedly never lit. It is an OVERRIDE id (428522) that replaces Hand of
--     Gul'dan while the proc is up -- Profiles.lua says so -- and an override has no cooldown
--     of its own, so `ready(428522)` may be answering for the base spell or reading UNKNOWN
--     and failing dark. `/sg why` on the row during a proc is the test; if it reads UNKNOWN,
--     the rung wants the proc window itself, not readiness.
--   * Shadow Bolt (686) and its override Infernal Bolt (434506) are ONE row, and this file
--     now puts a glow on each. Confirm `on shadow_bolt` binds while the row shows Shadow
--     Bolt, and watch both across a Mother of Chaos proc -- the pair must not light together.
--   * Nothing here rests on the duration curve's unit. SECONDS is already measured: a
--     `> 30s` mark went dark at thirty seconds remaining on a ~90s cooldown, which a
--     millisecond domain would have dropped at 30ms and a [0, 1] one would never have lit
--     (backlog.md). protection-durationprobe.sg's header still says the unit is unmeasured;
--     it predates that flight and is wrong.
